    <string name="ui_after_connecting_the_phone_enters_landscape_desktop_tap" formatted="false">"After connecting, the phone enters landscape desktop. Tap to control, drag to move content, long-press for mouse right-click, two fingers to zoom or pan. The three floating buttons at the top control zoom/restore, session menu and keyboard. With the keyboard open, use two fingers to move and view occluded areas; the session menu can open Task Manager, the Windows Start menu, restore the full desktop, or disconnect and return."</string>
    <string name="ui_after_switching_apps_or_locking_the_screen_the_connecti" formatted="false">"After switching apps or locking the screen, the connection is kept according to the “Background retention” setting for 1, 2 or 5 minutes and shows a notification; return in time to continue, otherwise the connection is released after the timeout. The system may also end background apps early. To release the phone connection immediately, tap “Disconnect and exit” in settings. After the remote desktop disconnects, programs on the computer keep running. The app does not register auto-start and does not use the Android VPN interface."</string>
